# 3. Inheritance — GeometricObject, Circle, Rectangle

```java
public class TestGeometricObject {

    public static void main(String[] args) {

        // Create a Circle object with radius 5.
        Circle circle = new Circle(5);


        // Create a Rectangle object.
        //
        // width = 4
        // height = 6
        Rectangle rectangle = new Rectangle(4, 6);


        // Circle does NOT directly contain setColor().
        //
        // However, Circle EXTENDS GeometricObject.
        //
        // Therefore Circle inherits the public
        // setColor() method from GeometricObject.
        circle.setColor("Red");


        // Rectangle also extends GeometricObject,
        // so Rectangle can also use setColor().
        rectangle.setColor("Blue");


        System.out.println("CIRCLE");

        // getColor() was inherited from GeometricObject.
        System.out.println("Color: " + circle.getColor());

        // getArea() belongs to Circle.
        System.out.println("Area: " + circle.getArea());


        System.out.println();


        System.out.println("RECTANGLE");

        // Inherited from GeometricObject.
        System.out.println("Color: " + rectangle.getColor());

        // Defined inside Rectangle.
        System.out.println("Area: " + rectangle.getArea());
    }
}


// SUPERCLASS / PARENT CLASS
//
// Circle and Rectangle will inherit from this class.
class GeometricObject {

    // Private data field.
    //
    // Since it is private, subclasses cannot
    // directly access color.
    //
    // They can still use the public
    // getter and setter.
    private String color;


    // Constructor for GeometricObject.
    public GeometricObject() {

        // Default color.
        color = "White";
    }


    // Getter.
    public String getColor() {
        return color;
    }


    // Setter.
    public void setColor(String color) {

        // this.color = object's data field
        //
        // color = parameter
        this.color = color;
    }
}


// SUBCLASS / CHILD CLASS
//
// "extends GeometricObject" creates inheritance.
//
// Circle IS-A GeometricObject.
class Circle extends GeometricObject {

    // Data specifically needed by Circle.
    private double radius;


    // Circle constructor.
    public Circle(double radius) {

        this.radius = radius;
    }


    // Calculate circle area.
    public double getArea() {

        // Formula:
        //
        // πr²
        return Math.PI * radius * radius;
    }
}


// SUBCLASS / CHILD CLASS
//
// Rectangle IS-A GeometricObject.
class Rectangle extends GeometricObject {

    private double width;
    private double height;


    public Rectangle(double width, double height) {

        this.width = width;
        this.height = height;
    }


    public double getArea() {

        return width * height;
    }
}
```

### Inheritance Structure

```text
             GeometricObject
             SUPERCLASS
             /        \
            /          \
       Circle        Rectangle
      SUBCLASS       SUBCLASS
```

Remember:

```java
class Circle extends GeometricObject
```

means:

```text
Circle IS-A GeometricObject
```

