# 6. Interface Example

```java
public class InterfaceExample {

    public static void main(String[] args) {

        // Create a Dog object.
        Dog dog = new Dog();


        // Dog has makeSound() because Dog
        // implements the Animal interface.
        dog.makeSound();
    }
}


// INTERFACE
//
// An interface is like a contract.
//
// It says:
// "Any class that implements me must provide
// these required methods."
interface Animal {

    // This declares the method.
    //
    // It says classes implementing Animal
    // need a makeSound() method.
    void makeSound();
}


// Dog agrees to follow the Animal interface.
//
// IMPORTANT:
//
// Classes EXTEND classes.
//
// Classes IMPLEMENT interfaces.
class Dog implements Animal {

    // Since Dog implements Animal,
    // Dog provides the required makeSound() method.
    public void makeSound() {

        System.out.println("Woof!");
    }
}
```

### MEMORIZE

```java
class Child extends Parent
```

means:

```text
INHERITANCE
```

While:

```java
class Dog implements Animal
```

means:

```text
INTERFACE
```

