# 9. Loop Through an Array

```java
public class ArrayLoopExample {

    public static void main(String[] args) {

        // Create an array containing five integers.
        int[] numbers = {
            10, 20, 30, 40, 50
        };


        // Start i at 0 because arrays begin
        // at index 0.
        //
        // Continue while:
        //
        // i < numbers.length
        //
        // numbers.length = 5
        //
        // Therefore i will become:
        //
        // 0
        // 1
        // 2
        // 3
        // 4
        //
        // It stops before i becomes 5.
        for (
            int i = 0;
            i < numbers.length;
            i++
        ) {

            // numbers[i] accesses the element
            // at the current index.
            //
            // When i = 0:
            //
            // numbers[0] = 10
            //
            // When i = 1:
            //
            // numbers[1] = 20
            System.out.println(
                "Index " + i +
                " contains " + numbers[i]
            );
        }


        // NEVER normally use:
        //
        // i <= numbers.length
        //
        // because if length = 5,
        // that allows i to become 5.
        //
        // But index 5 does NOT exist.
        //
        // Valid indexes are only:
        //
        // 0, 1, 2, 3, 4
    }
}
```

